  "_README": [
    "A RATCHET BASELINE, not an allowlist. Every count here is a finding nobody has",
    "fixed yet; the file exists so the number can only go DOWN. `coord lint-fail-loud`",
    "compares the live scan against it and names each (file, pattern) whose count grew.",
    "It is tracked on purpose: the lint module's own allowlist lives under the gitignored",
    ".coordharness/ state directory, so a gate driven by that allowlist is vacuous in a",
    "fresh checkout or in CI -- the same defect that got cwd_relative_paths left unwired.",
    "Scope is src/coordharness only. The module's own SRC_ROOT is the repository ROOT,",
    "which walks .venv (310 findings, third-party) and build/ (167, a byte copy of src",
    "counted twice); that is why the headline number was 686 and the actionable one is 167.",
    "Keys are file::pattern, not file:line: moving code down a file is not a regression,",
    "and a second silent failure in a file that already had one is.",
    "Frozen against the COMMITTED tree at frozen_at_commit, scanned from a clean checkout;",
    "uncommitted work in any worktree therefore shows up as a regression, which is the point."
  ],
